To complete what you're saying: by the time you've reached the
endgame, there are basically two types of monsters in nethack,
those you can melee, and those you don't want to let close to
you.  For the latter, Magicbane's extra effects are worthless,
since they only come into effect in melee.  For the first, you
should have enough hitpoints and AC that even a moderately good
melee weapon (which includes Magicbane at +6 or +7) is largely
sufficient, without any extra effects.

    [...]
> Even the lowly sleep spell is better in this case; it works
> _at range_, thus allowing you to keep a monster stationary and
> passive for deadination in its near future.  Magicbane's
> special effects all go off in melee, though, making
> (ironically) possibly its most valuable feature the defensive
> ones -- MR and infinite Elbereth.

Not to mention the fact that it absorbs most curses.  (And a
cursed bag of holding will slow you down enough to allow those
monsters that you don't want to melee to get close enough to
melee.)

For a wizard, the best strategy with regards to weapons is
clear: Magicbane, plus elvin daggers in the quiver, plus your
spells.

